# Catalog metadata acquisition\par
\par
License: GPL-3.0-only. See `COPYING`.\par
\par
Adapted from selected OneTagger providers vendored by CueRithm:\par
https://github.com/Marekkon5/onetagger\par
Base commit: `36523f71f2d9a5947912f3cb930f1a31fcb2e3ee`.\par
Beatport catalog API adaptation: OneTagger PR526, pinned by CueRithm at\par
`rosgr100/onetagger@f7adb26a2e0790b0ff751bee04a05c1c20dbd009`.\par
CueRithm donor revision: `cbc866c3b5bcc395906b5713f64f0dc53b05177c`.\par
CueRithm donor: `vendor/onetagger/providers/\{beatport,traxsource,http\}.rs`.\par
\par
Preserve the upstream GPL notice and license with redistribution. The upstream\par
authors retain their copyrights.\par
\par
This crate adapts catalog queries, metadata structures, Traxsource selectors,\par
challenge detection and the optional FlareSolverr-compatible transport. It adds\par
complete Traxsource releases, exact track-to-release navigation, application\par
pagination, bounded async requests and cancellation. It imports no tag writer,\par
matching engine, UI, audio library, browser cookies or executable hooks.\par
\par
All fixtures are invented minimal examples. No captured HAR content, credentials\par
from a browser, or user data is included. The upstream-distributed Beatport public\par
application credentials are catalog application identifiers, not user credentials.\par
The host supplies proxy/timeout/TLS/redirect policy and offline endpoint routing.\par
Solver requests contain only a public catalog URL and timeout; solver use is opt-in.\par
Challenge state and the Beatport token are retained only in application memory.\par
\par
Validation uses parsers and loopback HTTP fixtures; it makes no live catalog calls.\par
